Superpermutation upper bounds

This repository presents the improved upper construction from Jay Pantone's
superpermutation research. The underlying completion, transport, connector,
and word-assembly library accompanies:
https://github.com/jaypantone/superperm-upper-43-80

The proof sources and explicit words were curated from the combined release
https://github.com/jaypantone/2026-10-superpermutation-bounds
at commit c9ccb6a0d9ddd1007fdce6efab50807ec47464b9. That source snapshot may
remain private; the substantive supporting proofs needed by this repository
are included here. This is a migration and submission package for the same
mathematical results, not a claim of an additional improvement.

Jakub Halfar's finite selections and replacement construction contribute to
the general upper bound. The explicit words also build on his selections
X, E and N, and the ten-symbol word follows the mixed-trail organization
contributed by rumstd to the earlier repository. The paper and
words/README.md identify the inherited ingredients and the improvements.
Halfar's construction repository is:
https://github.com/jhalfar/superpermutations

The sources, paper, word files, and certificates are distributed under
Apache License 2.0. Existing source notices are preserved. Lean and Mathlib
are external dependencies with their own licenses and notices.
